cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this reduced-order architecture, the D067-ART-v1 package, or
  the source monograph, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  Adaptive-Resonance-Tracked Phononic Piezoelectric Light Source: From 100
  Phononic Metacrystals to D067-ART-v1 Adaptive Resonance Tracking
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Lockwood
    given-names: James
date-released: "2026-09-01"
version: D067-ART-v1
repository-code: "https://github.com/Blaze61029dogQ-pixel/Chronomagnetics"
abstract: >-
  An extended computational monograph documenting a local-compute design
  program that screened 100 phononic metacrystal families, converted the
  strongest candidate (D067) into a finite electromechanical light-source
  model, audited it independently, closed the electromechanical coupling
  and capacitance physically against PZT-5A material data, and rejected a
  passive fixed-frequency production architecture on manufacturing-corner
  robustness grounds. The frozen result, D067-ART-v1, is a nested inertial
  phononic resonator coupled to a PZT-5A transducer with adaptive
  resonance tracking and adaptive electrical loading. Status: reduced-order
  architecture freeze, not experimentally validated.
keywords:
  - phononic metacrystals
  - piezoelectric energy harvesting
  - adaptive resonance tracking
  - reduced-order modeling
  - PZT-5A
